Offshore Waters Forecast

NWS National Hurricane Center Miami, FL

142 PM PDT Sat Aug 2 2025



Offshore Waters Forecast for the E Pacific within 250 nm of

Central America, Colombia, and within 750 nm of Ecuador



Seas given as significant wave height, which is the average

height of the highest 1/3 of the waves. Individual waves may be

more than twice the significant wave height.



PMZ101-030845-

Synopsis for the E Pacific within 250 nm of Central America,

Colombia, and within 750 nm of Ecuador

142 PM PDT Sat Aug 2 2025



.SYNOPSIS...Gap winds across the Papagayo region will pulse 

moderate to fresh through Mon, then will weaken late Tue through

Wed. Light to gentle winds will prevail elsewhere N of the 

monsoon trough through early Tue, then become fresh to strong 

late Tue through Wed with the passage of a tropical wave. Gentle

to moderate winds can be expected S of the monsoon trough. New 

SW swell will move through the regional waters this weekend, 

then slowly subside by Mon. Yet another pulse of SW swell will 

raise seas across the regional waters Tue through Wed.



$$



