Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Utah

National Weather Service Salt Lake City UT

243 PM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025



...RED FLAG WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM MDT THIS

EVENING FOR WIND AND LOW RELATIVE HUMIDITY FOR FIRE WEATHER ZONES

483, 484, 488, 489, 493, 494, 496, AND 498...

...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT FROM NOON MONDAY TO 9 PM MDT

TUESDAY FOR WIND AND LOW RELATIVE HUMIDITY FOR FIRE WEATHER ZONES

483, 484, 488, 489, 492, 493, 494, 495, 496, 497, AND 498...



.BROADCAST DISCUSSION...A warm and very dry airmass will remain 

across the region through early next week, bringing very low 

RH with poor overnight recovery. Widespread critical fire weather 

conditions are expected across portions of central and southern 

Utah Saturday and again through most of next week. 



.DISCUSSION...A hot, dry airmass will remain in place through the

next week. As high pressure moves overhead Sunday, winds will 

decrease across the region...however...winds will increase once 

again Monday as southwest flow increases once more. Widespread 

critical fire weather conditions are expected across central and 

southern Utah. Localized critical fire weather conditions are 

likely across portions of fire weather zone 479, especially Monday

afternoon.



Mid-level moisture will increase Tuesday across southern Utah, 

but little increase in humidities is expected for areas below 8500

feet or so. Current guidance suggests most locations across 

central and southern Utah will remain in a prolonged period of 

critical fire weather conditions with poor to very poor overnight

recoveries through at least Thursday. 



***Thunderstorms imply strong, gusty and erratic winds***

***All winds are 20 foot, 10-minute averages***



