.DISCUSSION...Sunday and Monday...Hot, dry and occasionally windy 

conditions will continue. Daytime minimum relative humidity values 

ranging from 5 to 13 percent each day. Daytime winds southwesterly 

10 to 20 mph, with gusts from 25 to 30 mph Sunday, increasing to 15 

to 25 mph, with gusts as high as 35 mph on Monday.



Tuesday through Thursday...Hot and mostly dry conditions will 

continue. A minor increase in dew points from the south will raise 

minimum relative humidities to around 10 to 20 percent for each day. 

Only slight chances of showers or thunderstorms will develop over 

the higher terrain of central Arizona during this forecast period. 

The Kaiabab Plateau is likely to stay dry. Daytime southwest winds 

10 to 20 mph, with gusts around 25 mph, each day.



