Denver/Boulder Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2002 UTC Saturday, August  2, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS through 18Z Sunday/...

Issued at 1138 AM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025

Showers and thunderstorms will increase over the next couple of 

hours becoming scattered by 19-20Z. The showers/storms will mainly

be high-based with gusty outflows up to 45 knots. Wind shifts 

(possibly several) are possible 20z to 02Z. Any storm is expected

to be short-lived with brief heavy rain also possible.

The showers and thunderstorms end early to mid evening. Skies 

slowly clear overnight with mostly clear skies for Sunday. Winds 

become a southerly drainage direction this evening and stay 

southerly into Sunday morning. A dry cold front is expected to 

arrive around 15Z bringing a wind shift to the north.





