Goodland Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1946 UTC Saturday, August  2, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS THROUGH 18Z SUNDAY/...

Issued at 1111 AM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025

MVFR ceilings and minor reductions in smoke may persist into the

early afternoon at both KGLD and KMCK before clearing. VFR will

prevail through the afternoon and early evening before storms

move in from the west. If directly impacted by a thunderstorm,

either terminal could see brief gusty winds and reductions in

visibility in rain. A brief period of low clouds will be

possible around sunrise Sunday morning.



Dodge City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1955 UTC Saturday, August  2, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS THROUGH 18Z SUNDAY/...

Issued at 1221 PM CDT Sat Aug 2 2025

Southeast winds will be at 10 to 15 knots over the next 24 

hours. Tonight an area of thunderstorms will cross southwest 

Kansas. A few of the stronger storms will be capable of 

producing locally strong gusty winds, hail and locally heavy 

rainfall. Garden City and Liberal has the highest chance for 

these storms between 03z and 06z Sunday followed by Hays and 

Dodge City between 05z and 08z Sunday. Outside of these storms, 

VFR conditions are expected today and tonight, with ceilings 

occasionally as low as 5000ft AGL. After 12z Sunday HREF has a 

50% chance for ceilings to be 3000ft AGL, especially in the Hays

and Dodge City area.





