Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1839 UTC Saturday, August  2, 2025



.AVIATION...

(18Z TAFS)

Issued at 1111 AM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025

VFR currently ongoing this hour with another round of

thunderstorms expected to begin developing over the high terrain

b/w 18Z to 20Z. Isolated to scattered coverage of thunderstorms is

expected to roll off to the east of the respective mountain chains

over surrounding lower elevations 20Z thru 03Z. A few PROB30s are

included for KABQ and KSAF for mostly dry more shower activity 

that could produce gusty outflow winds. PROB30s at KLVS and KTCC 

have a slightly better chance for producing rainfall at these 

terminals alongside gusty outflow winds and some lightning 

strikes. Conditions calm and clear tonight into Sunday morning.

Stronger scattered storms potentially becoming severe will favor 

areas from KRTN to KCAO, perhaps as far south as KTCC this 

afternoon and early evening.



