738

FNUS55 KBOI 022051

FWFBOI



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for SW Idaho and SE Oregon

National Weather Service Boise ID

251 PM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025



...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 8 PM MDT /7 PM PDT/ THIS 

EVENING FOR LIGHTNING IN FIRE ZONES 423, 672, 673 AND 674...



...ISOLATED TO SCATTERED THUNDERSTORMS WITH WIDESPREAD GUSTY 

WINDS SUNDAY AFTERNOON AND EVENING... 



.DISCUSSION...

A low pressure system will bring another round of thunderstorms 

to the region on Sunday. Isolated to scattered thunderstorms 

will develop across southeast Oregon and the west-central Idaho 

mountains in the morning, continuing in this area through the 

afternoon. Thunderstorms will cross the lower Snake Plain and 

Boise mountains in the afternoon. Gusty outflow winds up 

to 65 mph are possible across east-central Oregon and portions of 

west-central Idaho. Outside of gusty thunderstorm winds, a cold 

frontal passage will bring widespread gusty winds of 30 to 45 mph 

that will impact most fire zones between late Sunday afternoon 

and Sunday evening. A chance of showers and thunderstorms remains 

on Monday before dry weather returns.





