2025-08-02T20-51-53-063Z

[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.4377","issue":"2025-08-02T20:51:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS65","cccc":"KGGW","awipsid":"AFDGGW"}]
=================================================



740

FXUS65 KGGW 022051

AFDGGW



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Glasgow MT

251 PM MDT Sat Aug 2 2025



.DISCUSSION...



KEY MESSAGES:



1) Scattered thunderstorms are expected between 4pm and midnight

with heavy rainfall, frequent lightning, and gusty winds possible.



2) An active pattern is expected to remain in place next week with

chances for showers and thunderstorms continuing at times and

seasonable temperatures.



WEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:



Isolated thunderstorms are already beginning to develop and will

become more scattered this afternoon and evening. HREF shows a

concentrated corridor from Valley County southeast to Dawson

County. The main concerns include heavy rainfall and frequent

lightning but an isolated wind gust over 50 mph cannot be ruled

out.



Higher resolution model data continues to show some support of low

concentrations of smoke in the vicinity over the next day,

especially east, so will continue to monitor.



Meanwhile, zonal or southwest flow over the next few days will

accompany an active weather pattern along with seasonable

temperatures over all. Longer term ensembles in fact point to a

decreasing trend in temperatures toward next weekend.



FORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:



NBM was largely followed this forecast cycle and handled

expectations well. Confidence remains high on thunderstorm chances

today but low on exact timing and locations. Lower confidence also

exists on where patchy smoke may present, though greater chances

look to exist off to the east into North Dakota per latest HRRR

smoke guidance.





&&



.AVIATION...



LAST UPDATED: August 2, 2025 at 2045Z



FLIGHT CAT RANGE: VFR. 



DISCUSSION: 

VFR conditions will continue to prevail tonight. That said,

scattered thunderstorms may produce brief IFR/MVFR visibilities

and reduced ceilings. Patchy haze and smoke may also present at

times.



WIND: Expect light and variable winds overall tonight, though

gusty and shifting winds are possible near storms. 





&&



.GGW WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

None.

&&



$$



weather.gov/glasgow



