755

FNUS85 KVEF 022052

FWLVEF



ECCDA DISCUSSIONS

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE LAS VEGAS NV

152 PM PDT SAT AUG 2 2025



#####################################################################

##                                                                 ##

##            DISCUSSIONS FROM THE LATEST FWF BELOW                ##

##                                                                 ##

#####################################################################



...DISCUSSION FROM RNOFWFVEF...



DRY AND BREEZY CONDITIONS WILL CONTINUE THROUGH EARLY NEXT WEEK WITH

FAIRLY SEASONABLE TEMPERATURES. AFERNOON MIN RH WILL DROP INTO THE

SINGLE DIGITS DAILY OUTSIDE OF THE VERY HIGHEST ELEVATIONS.

TEMPERATURES WILL BEGIN TO CLIMB MID TO LATE WEEK AS HIGH PRESSURE

STREGNTHENS OVER THE REGION. 





...DISCUSSION FROM LAXFWFSGX...





DRY CONDITIONS ARE EXPECTED TO PREVAIL THROUGH THE FORECAST  PERIOD

WITH HOT CONDITIONS FOR THE MIDDLE TO END OF THE UPCOMING  WEEK.

THROUGH TUESDAY, NEAR NORMAL TEMPERATURES ARE EXPECTED FOR  MOST

LOCATIONS WITH THE DESERTS RUNNING UP TO 5 DEGREES ABOVE  AVERAGE.

MINIMUM AFTERNOON RELATIVE HUMIDITY OF 5 TO 15 PERCENT IN THE

MOUNTAINS AND DESERTS WITH TYPICAL AFTERNOON SEA BREEZES  GUSTING TO

AROUND 35 MPH BELOW THE PASSES. WARMER CONDITIONS  EXPECTED

WEDNESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY, WITH TEMPERATURES RUNNING 5  TO

10 DEGREES ABOVE AVERAGE. THERE IS SOME INCREASE IN MID-LEVEL 

MOISTURE DURING THIS PERIOD, BUT SHOWER/THUNDERSTORM CHANCES  REMAIN

BELOW 10%. THE MARINE LAYER DEPTH WILL FLUCTUATE BETWEEN 

1000-1500 FT THROUGH MUCH OF THE FORECAST PERIOD. 





...DISCUSSION FROM PHXFWFPSR...





DRIER CONDITIONS WILL CONTINUE TO SETTLE IN THIS WEEKEND WITH ONLY A

SMALL CHANCE FOR AN ISOLATED SHOWER OR THUNDERSTORM ACROSS SOUTHERN

GILA COUNTY THIS AFTERNOON. MIN RHS WILL FALL INTO THE 5-10% RANGE

THIS WEEKEND, WHILE MAX RHS RANGE BETWEEN 20-30% FOR MOST AREAS.

WINDS WILL GENERALLY FOLLOW DIURNAL TENDENCIES WITH  TYPICAL

AFTERNOON UPSLOPE GUSTINESS. TEMPERATURES WILL REMAIN  ABOVE NORMAL

WITH LOWER DESERT HIGHS MOSTLY BETWEEN 108-114  DEGREES.





#####################################################################

