Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1400 PDT on August 02. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



Please contact National Weather Service Elko if you have questions

or concerns with this forecast.



.DISCUSSION...Main concern this afternoon will be contiued isolated

dry thunderstorms in the area. Cloud to ground lightning along 

with gusty and erratic outflow winds of 45+ mph should be expected

with any storms that move in vicinity. Storms dissipate and skies

clear tonight with winds shifting northerly as nocturnal downslopes

develop. Thunderstorms not expected Sunday though afternoon

breezes will be present with gusts 20 to 25 mph. 



