Hazardous Weather Outlook

National Weather Service Wichita KS

404 PM CDT Sat Aug 2 2025



KSZ032-033-047>053-067>072-082-083-091>096-098>100-032115-

Russell-Lincoln-Barton-Ellsworth-Saline-Rice-McPherson-Marion-Chase-

Reno-Harvey-Butler-Greenwood-Woodson-Allen-Kingman-Sedgwick-Harper-

Sumner-Cowley-Elk-Wilson-Neosho-Chautauqua-Montgomery-Labette-

404 PM CDT Sat Aug 2 2025



This hazardous weather outlook is for portions of Central Kansas,

South Central Kansas and Southeast Kansas.



.DAY ONE...Tonight



Areas of smoke from Canadian wildfires will continue to reduce 

visibility as low as 4 miles across the entire area this afternoon

and evening.



Better thunderstorm chances will arrive late tonight with a few 

strong storms possible.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Sunday through Friday



A few strong to marginally severe storms possible Sunday afternoon

into Sunday evening.



Heat indices above 100 will return on Wednesday across southern

Kansas and will last through Friday each afternoon.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation is not anticipated tonight.



