Offshore Waters Forecast

NWS Ocean Prediction Center Washington DC

505 PM EDT Sat Aug 2 2025



West central North Atlantic continental shelf and slope waters

beyond 20 nm to 250 nm offshore, including south of Georges Bank

from 1000 fm to 250 nm offshore.



Seas given as significant wave height, which is the average

height of the highest 1/3 of the waves. Individual waves may be

more than twice the significant wave height.



Locally higher winds and seas can be expected in and near tstms.



ANZ899-030915-

505 PM EDT Sat Aug 2 2025



.SYNOPSIS FOR MID ATLC WATERS...Low pressure off the SE coast will

move NE along a stationary front over the central waters tonight

through Mon, while pulling a cold front over the S waters. The 

low will pass E of the area by Mon night. The cold front will 

become nearly stationary and linger over the S waters Tue through

Thu night with weak lows occasionally forming along the frontal 

boundary. High pressure over the N waters will continue over 

those parts into next week. A stronger high will build N of the 

area Tue night into Thu night. All mariners should use caution in

or near any of the heavier thunderstorms which will likely 

persist mainly near and S of the cold front today through Sun. 



$$



