Washington Park   N/A    N/A       N/A        N/A         N/A





Abbreviations and Definitions... 



Flags 



Green: Generally safe to swim 

Yellow: Caution is urged 

Red: Hazardous to swim



Currents Present (if any) As Reported by Lifeguards or Park Rangers 

RIP: Rip current-Powerful channels of water flowing quickly away 

from the shore. They occur most often at low spots or breaks in 

sandbars. Rip currents can sweep you into deeper water.



LON: Longshore Current-A lake current that moves parallel to shore. 

It can be strong enough to prevent swimmers from being able to keep 

their feet on the bottom... making it difficult to return to shore.



STR: Structural Current-A lake current that forms along piers where 

longshore currents and wave action flow into the structure.

Structural currents can sweep you out into deeper water along the 

pier structure.



N/A: No report of that variable (currents, temp, waves, and flag 

color) available. If no reports are available from a beach, the line 

will be deleted from the OMR.



NONE: No currents were observed



