Fire Weather Planning Forecast for NE Oregon and SE Washington

National Weather Service Pendleton OR

748 AM PDT Sun Aug 3 2025



...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT FROM 2 PM THIS AFTERNOON TO 8 PM

PDT THIS EVENING FOR ABUNDANT LIGHTNING FOR FIRE WEATHER ZONE

OR698...



...SCATTERED THUNDERSTORMS TODAY CENTRAL OREGON AND EASTERN 

MOUNTAINS...



.DISCUSSION...Scattered wet and isolated dry thunderstorms will

develop across Central Oregon, Eastern Mountains, and along the

Blue Mountain foothills today. Greatest threat for dry

thunderstorms will be in the southern Blues this afternoon. 

Isolated storms will continue across the eastern mountains 

through early Monday evening. Locally breezy winds will develop 

through the Cascade gaps each afternoon into the midweek. Dry 

conditions briefly return Tuesday before afternoon RHs trend 

higher through the week.





***Thunderstorms imply strong gusty winds***

***Winds are 20 foot 10 minute averages***

***CWR-chance of wetting rain 0.10 or greater***

***Ventilation Index is derived from the

   transport wind multiplied by the mixing

   height in 100's of feet. Index categories

   are a generalized indicator and users are

   encourage to develop criteria that are 

   suitable and representative of dispersion

   conditions in their local area of interest.***

     Note: Max transport winds may not occur 

     at the same time as max mixing height. 



