FNUS75 KMSO 031458

FWSMSO



Spot Forecast for Boat

National Weather Service Missoula MT

858 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0913 MDT on August 03. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...Chance for showers or thunderstorms between 1500-2000

MDT today. Direct impact from largely hit-or-miss strong shower 

or storm could produce erratic gusts up to 35 mph. Wetting rain / 

upper end precip amount based on direct impact from heavy shower 

or storm. More clouds with better chance/increased coverage of wetting

rain/heavy shower Monday afternoon and evening between 1400-2000 

MDT, a direct impact from strong storm could produce erratic gusts

up to 40 mph. 10% chance to see 0.33" or more Monday afternoon.



.REST OF TODAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Mostly sunny becoming partly cloudy with a

  chance for showers and thunderstorms in the afternoon and

  evening.

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...15 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....30 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....74-79. 

* Min Humidity........15-20 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/south 2-5 mph with gusts up to 10

  mph in the morning becoming west 3-6 mph with gusts up to 15 mph

  in the afternoon. Direct impact from shower or storm could

  produce erratic gusts up to 35 mph.

* Mixing Height.......Near 2500 ft agl in the morning increasing

  to near 11000 ft agl in the afternoon.

* Mixing Winds........West-southwest 10 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.00-0.03 inches. 



.TONIGHT...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Chance of showers and 

  thunderstorms in the evening, then slight chance of rain 

  overnight. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...30 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....30 percent. 

* Min Temperature.....49-54. 

* Max Humidity........57-62 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........West-southwest 3-6 mph with gusts up to 15

  mph in the evening. Direct impact from storm could produce 

  erratic gusts up to 35 mph. Becoming south/variable 2-4 mph 

  overnight. 

* Mixing Height.......Decreasing to less than 1000 ft agl

  overnight.

* Mixing Winds........Southwest 7 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.00-0.17 inches. 



.MONDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Rain showers likely and chance 

  of thunderstorms in the afternoon. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...70 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....70 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....70-75. 

* Min Humidity........30-35 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/south 2-4 mph becoming west-

  northwest 3-7 mph with gusts up to 20 mph in the afternoon.

  Direct impact from strong storm could produce erratic gusts up

  to 40 mph.

* Mixing Height.......Near 1000 ft agl in the morning increasing

  to near 6000 ft agl in the afternoon.

* Mixing Winds........West 12 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.09-0.28 inches. 



