[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.4393","issue":"2025-08-03T15:05:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS63","cccc":"KMKX","awipsid":"AFDMKX"}]
=================================================



118

FXUS63 KMKX 031505

AFDMKX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Milwaukee/Sullivan WI

1005 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Wildfire smoke will create haze and air quality at unhealthy

  levels at times again today.



- Humidity gradually returns next week, along with shower and

  thunderstorm chances. 



&&



.UPDATE...

Issued 1005 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Elevated and near surface smoke remains across southern Wisconsin. 

High pressure has made skies clear and winds light and variable. So 

while the temperatures are pleasant and the skies are clear, 

there is not much air movement. So no major changes here.



Patterson



&&



.SHORT TERM...

Issued 355 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Today and Tonight:



It will be quiet again today under high pressure, with plenty of

sunshine and light winds expected along with near normal high 

temperatures. The main weather concern will be lingering 

wildfire smoke under the high. The latest HRRR suggests both 

elevated and near surface smoke may hang in into at least 

Monday. The Air Quality Advisory issued by the Wisconsin DNR 

remains in effect until noon today, with a further extension of

the advisory possible given the latest smoke forecast. 



DDV



&&



.LONG TERM...

Issued 355 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Monday through Saturday:



High pressure will continue to push east over eastern Ontario 

and gradually into Quebec. The high will slow fairly 

significantly and strengthen which will keep higher pressure 

across WI. This will likely keep conditions dry through at least

Tuesday. Into Wednesday while higher pressure may linger an 

upper level shortwave may slide through with a return of more 

direct southerly flow. This will allow for increased moisture 

and PWATs. The shortwave aloft whether we get showers and storms

or not as it pushes through looks likely to usher in upper 

level ridging across the area. This may also usher in a more 

active weather pattern with shortwaves riding the ridge into the

region. Exactly how this all unfolds is uncertain but the 

second half of next week looks much warmer and more humid with 

better chances for storms.



Kuroski



DDV



&&



.AVIATION...

Issued 1005 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



MVFR to VFR conditions will persist again through the day time with 

LIFR to VFR conditions expected overnight. Today will be very 

similar to the days prior with high pressure overhead. Partly cloudy 

to mostly clear skies and smoky conditions. Near surface smoke and 

smoke aloft remain with visibilites around 5 to 10 SM expected.

Winds are light and variable and temperatures are pleasant. 

Heading into tonight fog looks to return again. Terminals in low

lying areas, especially those in an around the Wisconsin River 

Valley, can expected visibilites to drop again to around 1-3 SM 

overnight into early Monday. As the high pressure overhead 

begins to pull east for the start of the work week, we can 

expect much of the same again Monday.



Patterson



&&



.MARINE...

Issued 355 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



High pressure around 30.2 inches will sit over the Great Lakes 

through early this week, bringing light and variable winds to 

Lake Michigan. Winds will gradually become east to southeast by 

mid- week as the high slowly shifts eastward, with southerly 

winds likely towards the end of the week ahead of an approaching

trough. 



DDV



&&



.MKX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

WI...None.

LM...None.

&&



$$



