North Platte Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1151 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION /12Z TAFS THROUGH 12Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 647 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025

VFR conditions are expected through the daytime Sunday for area

terminals.

Afternoon diurnal cumulus will interrupt the stream of high

level clouds with primary impacts at LBF. Scattered afternoon

convection appears likely to split the terminals and so will

keep mention out of VTN and cover with a TEMPO group at LBF late

tonight. Heavy rain will be the main concern with thunderstorms

at LBF and believe IFR conditions are possible under the

heaviest cores.

After convection clears out, expect expansive low-stratus to

develop across the area. This should remain south of VTN but

include LBF and have included a mention of IFR CIGs through the

end of the valid forecast period to cover the threat.





