493

FZNT32 KNHC 031515

OFFN21



Marine Weather HF Voice Broadcast

NWS National Hurricane Center Miami, FL

1115 AM EDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Marine Weather HF Voice Broadcast for the Gulf of America



Seas given as significant wave height, which is the average

height of the highest 1/3 of the waves. Individual waves may be

more than twice the significant wave height.



.SYNOPSIS...A frontal boundary will remain nearly stationary

across the northern Gulf region through at least Tue, generating

scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms. Wind and seas

could be higher near thunderstorms. A weak low pressure is

forecast to persist along the front in the vicinity of SE

Louisiana. Elsewhere, a weak ridge will prevail supporting

mostly gentle to moderate winds and slight to moderate seas.

Pulsing fresh E winds are likely at night north and west of the

Yucatan Peninsula, Mon night through Wed night, as a trough

develops there daily and drifts westward. 



Gulf of America N of 26N W of 87W



.THIS AFTERNOON...W winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TONIGHT...NW winds less than 10 kt, shifting to SE after

midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON...SW winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less.

.MON NIGHT...SE winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE...S winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE NIGHT...Variable winds less than 10 kt, becoming SE less

than 10 kt after midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.WED...SE winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.WED NIGHT...Variable winds less than 10 kt, becoming SE less

than 10 kt after midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU...SE winds less than 10 kt in the morning, becoming

variable winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU NIGHT...Variable winds less than 10 kt, becoming SE less

than 10 kt after midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 



Gulf of America from 22N to 26N W of 87W



.THIS AFTERNOON...Variable winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or

less. 

.TONIGHT...N winds less than 10 kt, shifting to SE after

midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON...S winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON NIGHT...SE winds less than 10 kt, increasing to 10 to 15 kt

after midnight. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE...SE winds 10 to 15 kt, diminishing to less than 10 kt in

the afternoon. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt, increasing to 10 to 15 kt

after midnight. Seas 2 ft or less, building to 3 ft after

midnight. 

.WED...SE winds 10 to 15 kt, diminishing to less than 10 kt in

the afternoon. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 3 ft. 

.THU...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 3 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 3 ft. 



SW Gulf of America S of 22N W of 87W



.THIS AFTERNOON...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TONIGHT...SE winds less than 10 kt within 60 nm of coast of

Veracruz, and NE 10 to 15 kt elsewhere. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt within 60 nm of coast of

Veracruz, and NE 10 to 15 kt elsewhere. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 2 ft or less, building to 3 ft

in the afternoon. 

.TUE NIGHT...NE winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 2 ft or less, building

to 3 to 4 ft after midnight. 

.WED...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...NE winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU...SE winds 10 to 15 kt, shifting to E in the afternoon.

Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less,

building to 3 ft after midnight. 



