Marine Weather HF Voice Broadcast

NWS National Hurricane Center Miami, FL

1115 AM EDT Sun Aug 3 2025



Marine Weather HF Voice Broadcast for the Tropical N Atlantic

from 07N to 19N W of 55W, the N Atlantic from 19N to

31N W of 55W including the Bahamas, and the Caribbean Sea.



Seas given as significant wave height, which is the average

height of the highest 1/3 of the waves. Individual waves may be

more than twice the significant wave height.



Synopsis for Caribbean Sea and Tropical N Atlantic from

07N to 19N W of 55W



.SYNOPSIS...The pressure gradient between the Atlantic high

pressure and the Colombia low will continue to allow for fresh

to strong winds and rough seas over the south-central Caribbean

mainly at night through Wed night. The strongest winds will

occur off the coast of Colombia, occasionally pulsing to near

gale-force at night. Moderate to fresh trades over the E

Caribbean will diminish to gentle to moderate speeds Tue morning

and then continue through Thu night. Moderate or weaker winds

over the NW Caribbean will reach moderate to fresh speeds Mon

night into Wed as a tropical wave moves across the W Caribbean

and Central America. 



NW Caribbean W of 85W



.THIS AFTERNOON...Variable winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or

less. 

.TONIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.TUE...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.TUE NIGHT...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 4 to 6 ft. 

.WED...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 4 to 6 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.THU...E winds 10 to 15 kt, diminishing to less than 10 kt in

the afternoon. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds less than 10 kt. Seas 3 ft. 



Caribbean N of 15N between 72W and 85W



.THIS AFTERNOON...E winds 10 to 15 kt S of 18N, and E less than

10 kt elsewhere. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.TONIGHT...E winds 10 to 20 kt S of 18N, and E less than 10 kt

elsewhere. S of 18N, seas 4 to 6 ft. Elsewhere, seas 2 ft or

less, building to 3 ft after midnight. 

.MON...S of 18N, E winds 10 to 20 kt. Elsewhere, E winds less

than 10 kt, increasing to 10 to 15 kt in the afternoon. Seas

5 to 7 ft S of 18N, and 3 ft elsewhere. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 5 to 7 ft S of 18N, and

3 to 5 ft elsewhere. 

.TUE...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 5 to 7 ft. 

.TUE NIGHT...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 4 to 6 ft. 

.WED...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 4 to 6 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.THU...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt, diminishing to less than 10 kt

after midnight. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 



Caribbean from 11N to 15N W of 72W



.THIS AFTERNOON...NE winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 5 to 6 ft. 

.TONIGHT...E winds 15 to 25 kt within 90 nm of coast of

Colombia, and NE 10 to 20 kt elsewhere. Seas 5 to 7 ft. 

.MON...E winds 15 to 25 kt. Seas 6 to 8 ft. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds 15 to 25 kt within 90 nm of coast of

Colombia, and E 10 to 20 kt elsewhere. Seas 6 to 8 ft. 

.TUE...E winds 10 to 20 kt. Seas 6 to 9 ft. 

