OFFN04



NAVTEX Marine Forecast

NWS National Hurricane Center Miami, FL

1119 AM EDT Sun Aug 3 2025



...Please refer to Coastal Waters Forecasts (CWF) available

through NOAA Weather Radio and other means for detailed

Coastal Waters Forecasts...



Southeast Gulf of America



.SYNOPSIS...A frontal boundary will remain nearly stationary

across the northern Gulf region through at least Tue, generating

scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms. Wind and seas

could be higher near thunderstorms. A weak low pressure is

forecast to persist along the front in the vicinity of SE

Louisiana. Elsewhere, a weak ridge will prevail supporting

mostly gentle to moderate winds and slight to moderate seas.

Pulsing fresh E winds are likely at night north and west of the

Yucatan Peninsula, Mon night through Wed night, as a trough

develops there daily and drifts westward.  



.THIS AFTERNOON...S winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TONIGHT...SE to S winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON...SE to S winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.MON NIGHT...SE winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE...SE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.TUE NIGHT...NE to E winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.WED...NE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.WED NIGHT...NE to E winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU...NE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less.  



Within 200 nm east of the coast of Florida



.SYNOPSIS...High pressure will dominate the weather pattern

through the period, supporting gentle to moderate anticyclonic

flow and slight to moderate seas mainly N of 25N. The northern

portion of a tropical wave, currently moving across the

Dominican Republic, will move across the remainder Hispaniola

this morning, reach the Turks and Caicos Islands today, and the

SE Bahamas tonight. The pressure gradient between the wave and

high pressure E of the Bahamas will support moderate to fresh

trades S of 25N during this period. 



.THIS AFTERNOON...S winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less, building

to 3 ft in the afternoon. Scattered showers and isolated tstms. 

.TONIGHT...E to SE winds 10 to 15 kt S of 27N, and S 5 to 10 kt N

of 27N. Seas 3 to 4 ft. Scattered showers and isolated tstms. 

.MON...SE to S winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.MON NIGHT...S of 27N, E winds 10 to 15 kt. N of 27N, NE to E

winds 5 to 10 kt, shifting to SE after midnight. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.TUE...SE winds 5 to 10 kt, shifting to NE to E in the afternoon.

Seas 3 ft. 

.TUE NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 ft. 

.WED...E winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 3 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E to SE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU...E to SE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less. 

.THU NIGHT...E to SE winds 5 to 10 kt. Seas 2 ft or less.



