NAVTEX Marine Forecast

NWS National Hurricane Center Miami, FL

1121 AM EDT Sun Aug 3 2025



...Please refer to Coastal Waters Forecasts (CWF) available

through NOAA Weather Radio and other means for detailed

Coastal Waters Forecasts...



.SYNOPSIS...A tropical wave currently moving across the Dominican

Republic will continue to generate showers across the regional 

waters through today. Otherwise, moderate to fresh E to SE winds 

across the regional waters will diminish to gentle to moderate 

speeds early Tue and then prevail the remainder forecast period. 

Also moderate seas will become slight on Tue. 



San Juan Atlantic Waters



.THIS AFTERNOON...SE winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.TONIGHT...E to SE winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.MON...E to SE winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.TUE...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.TUE NIGHT...NE to E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 4 ft. 

.WED...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU...E to SE winds 10 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft.  



San Juan Caribbean Waters



.THIS AFTERNOON...E to SE winds 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.TONIGHT...E winds 15 to 20 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.MON...E winds 15 to 20 kt. Seas 4 to 5 ft. 

.MON NIGHT...E winds 15 to 20 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.TUE...E winds 15 to 20 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.TUE NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.WED...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 5 ft. 

.WED NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft. 

.THU NIGHT...E winds 10 to 15 kt. Seas 3 to 4 ft.



