929 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025



This hazardous weather outlook is for northeast and north central

Colorado.



.DAY ONE...Today and Tonight



There will be a slight chance for thunderstorms this afternoon 

and evening over the plains of northern Colorado as well as the 

far eastern plains. Brief heavy rain, small hail, and wind gusts 

to 50 mph will be possible with the storms today. 



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Monday through Saturday



A drier airmass will be over the area next week. Temperatures 

will warm to above normal Monday and stay above normal for next 

week.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation will not be needed today or tonight.



$$



