Wood-Portage-Waupaca-Outagamie-Brown-Kewaunee-Waushara-Winnebago-

Calumet-Manitowoc-Southern Marinette County-

Southern Oconto County-

1029 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for north-central and northeast

Wisconsin.



.DAY ONE...This Afternoon and Tonight



Wildfire smoke from Canada will continue to impact air quality 

across the region. An Air Quality Advisory is currently in 

effect until noon Monday.



Patchy fog may reduce visibilities for motorists late tonight.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Monday through Saturday



Wildfire smoke from Canada will likely continue to impact air 

quality across the region early in the week. An Air Quality 

Advisory is currently in effect until noon Monday.



Thunderstorms are possible at times late in the week and into 

next weekend. It is too early to determine the severity of any 

thunderstorms.



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...



Spotter activation will not be needed this afternoon or tonight.



$$



LMZ521-522-541>543-041530-

The Bay of Green Bay south of a line from Cedar River MI to Rock

Island Passage-Lake Michigan from Washington Island to Sheboygan-

1029 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025



This Hazardous Weather Outlook is for portions of northwest Lake

Michigan and the waters of Green Bay.



.DAY ONE...This Afternoon and Tonight



The probability for widespread hazardous weather is low.



.DAYS TWO THROUGH SEVEN...Monday through Saturday



Thunderstorms are possible at times late in the week and into 

next weekend. Any thunderstorms could pose a hazard to mariners.



$$



