Riverton Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1439 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION /12Z TAFS THROUGH 12Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 407 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025

Drier air will push into the southwestern two thirds of the area

today, bringing mainly dry conditions. Mid level moisture will

hold on further northeast, so we have continued VCSH for KCPR

and added the group for KWRL as well. With more instability

across far northern Wyoming, we have added a PROB30 group for

thunder in vicinity of KCOD. Outside of any showers, conditions

will remain VFR through the period.



Cheyenne Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1111 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION /12Z TAFS THROUGH 12Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 508 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025

Mostly clear skies ongoing across the Wyoming terminals, while the 

Nebraska terminals are experiencing some mid-level clouds. Light, 

variable winds are ongoing across the region and will continue 

through about mid-morning. Winds increase mid-morning onwards. 

Primary aviation concern today will be isolated showers and storms 

producing strong winds and isolated large hail. Storms will be 

highly isolated in nature. Confidence is low on a storm directly 

impacting a terminal, due to their isolated nature. Expect gusty, 

erratic winds in and around any shower or storm that develops this 

afternoon.





