Goodland Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1055 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION /12Z TAFS THROUGH 12Z MONDAY/... 

Issued at 452 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025

The signal for stratus this morning has shifted slightly to the

east just far enough to take the MVFR ceilings out of the TAF; 

am starting to see some signs of the development just to the

south and east of MCK so will see how this pans out over the

next few hours. Winds are forecast to be lighter today around

6-10 knots. A severe storm remains possible for the GLD terminal

which would be capable of severe hail and strong to perhaps

damaging winds so will maintain the PROB30. A very strong signal

for stratus again Monday morning for MCK so have included in

this TAF; will need to monitor for westward expansion for GLD. 



Dodge City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1051 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION /12Z TAFS THROUGH 12Z MONDAY/...

Issued at 549 AM CDT Sun Aug 3 2025

Primarily VFR conditions are expected to prevail in vicinity of

all TAF sites through early evening. South-southeast winds around

10 to 20kt are forecast to persist through much of the period as

a lee side trough of low pressure remains anchored in extreme 

southeast Colorado.





