Albuquerque Aviation Discussion

Issued at 1129 UTC Sunday, August  3, 2025



.AVIATION...

(12Z TAFS)

Issued at 521 AM MDT Sun Aug 3 2025

Primarily MVFR, localized IFR, ceilings have developed in the 

wake of overnight thunderstorm activity over northeast NM. Attm, 

it appears this activity should remain east of KLVS and north of 

KTCC and erode by 16Z. VFR conditions are forecast this afternoon

through the evening hours. There is a very low chance for tstorms

to develop in the far ern plains of NM. If any develop, they will

be capable of large hail and damaging winds. Thereafter, expect a

sfc outflow boundary to push westward toward the central mts. It

appears low ceilings may develop in its wake, impacting KLVS and 

KTCC. Confidence is moderate, and thus, added SCT015 placeholders 

at these two terminals.



